  Orb of Fate, Magic Resistance (don't know if Janis had MR) and luck,
probably.  The Orb of Fate confers half physical damage as well has half
spell damage.  The only item in the game with both of those
characteristics.   

  You seem to have had impressive damage dealing abilities as well.
Maxed strength would have given +6 damage bonus for each weapon for a
total of 12 more points of damage.  Basic two-weapon would have given -2
total damage bonus.  Expert two-weapon would have given +2 total damage
bonus.

  Note the range of possible initial damage from Orcus psi bolt is 23 to
138.  There's one chance in 23^6 (~150,000,000) that it will do just 23
damage.  There's an equal chance it will do 138 damage, before modifiers
are taken into account.


  The range of results from the Orcus other attacks could also come into
it.  Starting with whether they hit at all, then how much damage they
try to do, and how much your armor manages to prevent.

  Even the movement system, where you start with a base speed and have
only a probability of extra movement based on whether you are "fast" or
"very fast."  You might have gotten the extra movement when you needed
and, and Janis might not.

  The movement system seems to be a place where the RNG can almost
invisibly kill your character.  Since the extra movement for being fast
or very fast is only a probability (and max two-thirds probability even
for very fast) you can easily not get it for several turns in a row.
Even for very fast there's an 11.1% chance you won't get any movement
boost two turns in a row.  Have that coincide with a little extra
damage, or multiple enemies, and poof, your character can be gone.
(Makes speed ascensions even more impressive, don't you think?)

  Remember, the monsters generally only have to kill your character
once.  You've got to survive pretty much every battle.


